# Typecheck gate · the last line before code reaches main.
#
# tsup/esbuild strip types, so `pnpm build` passes with real `tsc` errors and
# `pnpm lint` (biome) doesn't typecheck — `tsc --noEmit` is the only thing that
# catches that class. It runs here (pre-push), not pre-commit: full-monorepo tsc
# on every commit is too slow for that path, and push is the actual main-bound
# boundary we must defend. `turbo run typecheck` is content-cached, so this is
# ~instant when nothing relevant changed and only re-runs affected packages.
pnpm typecheck

# Test gate · added 2026-07-26 after the guardrail cell drifted from its workers
# through THREE commits without anything noticing. `hook-rule-boundary.test.ts`
# had been red the whole time; nothing ran it. A gate nobody runs is not a gate.
# turbo content-caches this to ~2s when nothing relevant changed.
pnpm test
